  "interpretation": "<p>The chromosome 21 analysis reveals the presence of an extra copy of chromosome 21, consistent with&nbsp;Trisomy 21 (Down syndrome). This genetic finding confirms the diagnosis and is associated with developmental delay and characteristic clinical features. Genetic counseling is recommended to discuss prognosis and recurrence risk.</p>\n<p>Chromosome 21 analysis shows a&nbsp;normal chromosomal pattern, with no evidence of trisomy, deletions, or structural abnormalities. There is&nbsp;no indication of Down syndrome or related genetic changes.</p>",
